playlist-checker (1.3.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: a playlist opened after another one was loaded but could stay
    invisible when a playlist / group filter, search or Show filter was
    active. Opening playlists now resets the list filters, and the status
    bar shows how many playlists and channels are loaded.
  * Playlists opened while a check is running are checked automatically as
    soon as that check ends.

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0300

playlist-checker (1.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: Check streams also checked and showed channels of unticked groups
    and playlists. Check streams, Recheck offline and the automatic check
    now skip them, and they are hidden from the channel list (click the
    group / playlist itself, or Show -> Excluded, to see them). Settings ->
    Hide unticked groups and playlists in the channel list (on by default).

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:20:00 +0300

playlist-checker (1.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: unticking groups or playlists did not change the totals.
    "All channels", "All playlists" and the counts per group / playlist now
    show the included channels (ticked group and ticked playlist), and the
    status bar and "Included: N of M" update at once.
  * Excluded channels are shown in grey; Show -> "Included (will be saved)"
    and "Excluded (unticked)".

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:10:00 +0300

playlist-checker (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Every playlist has its own color: a colored square on each channel row
    and a light row tint (Settings -> Tint rows with the playlist color).
    Duplicates stay yellow.
  * New "Playlists" list on the left: colors, channel and online counts;
    click to show only one playlist; untick to leave it out when saving.
  * Colors follow the order of the playlists in a URL list; direct stream
    links from a URL list belong to that list.

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0300

playlist-checker (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * File -> Open list of playlist URLs (.txt), Ctrl+L, also via Open files
    and the command line: downloads every playlist in the list (4 at a
    time, Stop cancels), adds direct stream links and local playlists, and
    lists the addresses that failed with the reason.
  * Addresses that return a single TV/radio stream (also HLS) are added as
    one channel instead of being downloaded as a playlist.
  * Settings -> Check new channels automatically after loading.
  * Example URL list in /usr/share/doc/playlist-checker/examples/.

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:45:00 +0300

playlist-checker (1.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Right-click menu (Cut, Copy, Paste, Delete, Select all) in every text
    field: Add from URL, Search, User-Agent and all dialogs.
  * Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V / Ctrl+X / Ctrl+A also work with Hebrew, Russian and
    other non-Latin keyboard layouts; Ctrl+A selects all.
  * Channel list: paste stream links or copied playlist text as new
    channels (right-click -> Paste, Ctrl+V, Edit menu); the right-click menu
    also opens on an empty list.

